"_doc": "Watch boxes for the 1972 Seiko V1 (JDM) catalogue: \"<page>:<k>\" (k = 1-based position of the record on its page, reading order) -> [x, y, w, h] normalised to the page, margin included; null = no photo. Oct 2026: the stock detector matched 94 of 123 pages (it splits bracelets and merges ring/pendant shots), so every box is set here: every caption in this catalogue starts with a blue bullet, so .pilot/1972-1972-seiko-v1/detect_bullets.py finds the bullets, takes each one's grid cell (printed rules, skew-tolerant) and boxes the photo ink above the caption; silver watches on coloured cloth (scan 3, 4, 73, 74) come from detect_colour_bg.py (low-saturation mask) and the fancy/stopwatch spreads (scan 121, 124, 128, 129, 131) were boxed by hand. All 670 boxes checked on per-page check sheets (final_check/).",
